## Key Changes

✅ **Added `originalLanguage` computed property**
- Extracts the raw language from code block before mapping
- Used to check original language in `showHTMLPreview`

✅ **Updated `showHTMLPreview` computed**
- Now checks `this.originalLanguage === 'html'` instead of mapped language
- Vue files will no longer show HTML preview option

✅ **Updated `buildFence` method**
- Uses `this.originalLanguage` to preserve original language in fence when rebuilding

This ensures:
- Only actual `html` blocks show the preview toggle
- `vue` blocks still show as HTML in the viewer but won't have preview option
- Mermaid and markdown blocks remain unaffected

I'll analyze the issue and fix it. The problem is that `selectedSize` is not being updated in the data when the select changes, so the watchers don't trigger properly.

Let me update the component:

```vue src/components/HTMLPreview.vue
<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="h-full flex flex-col">
    <div class="flex gap-2 p-2 border-b border-slate-500 flex-wrap items-center">
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium opacity-60">Screen:</span>
        <select 
          v-model="selectedSize" 
          class="select select-xs select-bordered max-w-xs"
          title="Select screen size"
        >
          <option value="custom">Custom</option>
          <option value="mobile-sm">Mobile (375px)</option>
          <option value="mobile-md">Mobile (425px)</option>
          <option value="tablet">Tablet (768px)</option>
          <option value="laptop">Laptop (1024px)</option>
          <option value="desktop">Desktop (1440px)</option>
          <option value="full">Full Width</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div v-if="selectedSize === 'custom'" class="flex gap-1 items-center">
        <input 
          v-model.number="customWidth" 
          type="number" 
          min="200" 
          max="2560"
          placeholder="Width"
          class="input input-xs input-bordered max-w-[80px]"
          title="Width in pixels"
        />
        <span class="text-xs opacity-60">×</span>
        <input 
          v-model.number="customHeight" 
          type="number" 
          min="200" 
          max="2560"
          placeholder="Height"
          class="input input-xs input-bordered max-w-[80px]"
          title="Height in pixels"
        />
        <span class="text-xs opacity-60">px</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-2 ml-auto">
        <button 
          class="btn btn-xs btn-outline"
          @click="refreshPreview"
          title="Refresh preview"
        >
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
          <span class="hidden sm:inline">Refresh</span>
        </button>
        <button 
          class="btn btn-xs btn-outline"
          @click="toggleFullscreen"
          title="Toggle fullscreen"
        >
          <i class="fa-solid fa-expand"></i>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-1 overflow-auto flex items-center justify-center p-4 bg-base-200" ref="previewContainer">
      <div 
        class="border border-slate-400 bg-white overflow-auto transition-all duration-200"
        :style="{ width: displayWidth + 'px', height: displayHeight + 'px' }"
      >
        <iframe
          ref="previewFrame"
          class="w-full h-full border-0"
          :key="refreshCounter"
          sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms"
          title="HTML Preview"
        ></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
const screenSizes = {
  'mobile-sm': { width: 375, height: 667 },
  'mobile-md': { width: 425, height: 812 },
  'tablet': { width: 768, height: 1024 },
  'laptop': { width: 1024, height: 768 },
  'desktop': { width: 1440, height: 900 },
  'full': { width: null, height: null }
}

export default {
  props: ['html'],
  data() {
    return {
      refreshCounter: 0,
      selectedSize: 'laptop',
      customWidth: 1024,
      customHeight: 768,
      displayWidth: 1024,
      displayHeight: 768
    }
  },
  watch: {
    html(newHtml) {
      this.$nextTick(() => {
        this.renderHTML(newHtml)
      })
    },
    selectedSize(newSize) {
      this.applySize(newSize)
    },
    customWidth(newVal) {
      if (this.selectedSize === 'custom') {
        this.displayWidth = newVal
      }
    },
    customHeight(newVal) {
      if (this.selectedSize === 'custom') {
        this.displayHeight = newVal
      }
    }
  },
  mounted() {
    this.applySize(this.selectedSize)
    this.renderHTML(this.html)
    window.addEventListener('resize', this.handleWindowResize)
  },
  beforeUnmount() {
    window.removeEventListener('resize', this.handleWindowResize)
  },
  methods: {
    renderHTML(htmlContent) {
      const iframe = this.$refs.previewFrame
      if (!iframe) return

      try {
        const doc = iframe.contentDocument || iframe.contentWindow.document
        doc.open()
        doc.write(`
          <!DOCTYPE html>
          <html>
          <head>
            <meta charset="UTF-8">
            <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
            <style>
              body {
                margin: 0;
                padding: 1rem;
                font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
                background-color: #0f172a;
                color: #e2e8f0;
              }
            </style>
          </head>
          <body>
            ${htmlContent}
          </body>
          </html>
        `)
        doc.close()
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Error rendering HTML preview:', error)
      }
    },

    applySize(sizeKey) {
      const size = screenSizes[sizeKey]
      if (sizeKey === 'full') {
        const container = this.$refs.previewContainer
        if (container) {
          this.displayWidth = container.clientWidth - 32
          this.displayHeight = container.clientHeight - 32
        }
      } else if (size) {
        this.displayWidth = size.width
        this.displayHeight = size.height
      }
    },

    refreshPreview() {
      this.refreshCounter++
      this.$nextTick(() => {
        this.renderHTML(this.html)
      })
    },

    toggleFullscreen() {
      const iframe = this.$refs.previewFrame
      if (!iframe) return

      if (iframe.requestFullscreen) {
        iframe.requestFullscreen()
      } else if (iframe.webkitRequestFullscreen) {
        iframe.webkitRequestFullscreen()
      }
    },

    handleWindowResize() {
      if (this.selectedSize === 'full') {
        this.applySize('full')
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

| Change | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Removed `@change="onSizeChange"` | No longer needed since watcher handles it |
| Added `selectedSize` watcher | Now triggers `applySize()` whenever size selection changes |
| Removed `onSizeChange()` method | Logic moved to watcher |
| Added `handleWindowResize()` method | Recalculates 'full' size when window resizes |
| Added window resize listener | Mounted and cleaned up properly |
| Added `transition-all duration-200` class | Smooth animation when size changes |

**What was wrong:**
- The `@change="onSizeChange"` event was firing but the method wasn't updating `selectedSize` in data, so the display dimensions weren't changing
- Now the watcher on `selectedSize` ensures that whenever the select changes, `applySize()` is called immediately

The preview will now properly resize when you select different screen sizes! 📱
